A||N||12||Jay||Northstar won't start||||1||
Z||000000||Jay||07-21-2001||02:29 PM||||Okay, yesterday I did something I have always said I will never do again.  I degreased my engine. (Last time I used a degreaser I shorted out my alternator on my prelude).  But I thought things would be different, Guess what... Now it won't start (The Northstar Fiero).    I changed wires, and DIS modual.  I've got spark.  The starter spins, the fuel pump primes.  Nothing.  It seems like it will start but it just doesn't "catch".  It will also backfire slightly.  The funny thing is the TPS keeps trying to adjust throttle and I get a ticking sound (from TPS pushing on throttle).  I can see the throttle moving as the TPS is pushing.  It keeps ticking even after the car is shut off.  Any ideas?  I'm thinking of pulling the plugs and putting in a freash set, since the plugs in there may be flooded.  I'm using Platinum 4's.  Thanks<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||California Kid||07-21-2001||03:14 PM||||Wish I could recommend where to look, but I don't know that much about the NorthStar to give you advise. <P>Certainly sounds like you have electrical connectors that aren't watertight. The best thing might be to let it set a day or two and it might just fine up like usual. I would recommend that after you have it running again, go to the local GM Dealership and pickup a tube of "electrical connector" grease. The find every connector you can locate and apply the grease to all internal contacts. Even though most of these connectors have seal boots, they don't alway work, I think the degreaser may break the surface tension of the water and allow it to get into places it wouldn't normally creap in to.<P>The first place I'd look is at all the electrical connections that were driven by the conversion.||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||07-21-2001||06:07 PM||||Well if you have sparkthe engine cranks over the pump is working.I would say that the motor is flooded how ever,You need to make sure that there is no gas in your oil. I f there is you should change the oil.when I lived in chicago years ago cars got flooded easily in the cold winters.I would change my oil first,then take four spark plugs out let them dry out a bit and crank the motor a couple of times to dry out the four cyl. then install the dry plugs .and that would ussually do the trick four me.I cant imagine how hard or easy it is to get to the back plugs .anyways I dont think you have a bad problem to deal with.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||07-21-2001||09:52 PM||||GM ECM's have a "flood clear" mode. Just hold the gas pedal on the floor while you crank. If it's flooded, that should fix it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||07-22-2001||03:22 AM||||I suppose it could be flooded, but it's very hard to flood an injected engine.  My bet is your spark is weak.  Sounds like you've gotten some moisture, etc. around the plug wires that's causing bad spark.  Try the old trick of WD40 on the DIS modules and around the plugs, etc.  This can displace water in distributors that have gotten waterlogged.  Maybe it'll help here.  Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000005||grinthock||07-22-2001||09:02 AM||||Hmmm That sucks Jay!!! Let us all know when it's fixed and what the problem is... It's still for sale right??||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jay||07-22-2001||03:26 PM||||Okay, I replaced all the plug wires installed a new DIS and replaced all 8 plugs.  Charged the battery overnight and nothing!!  It sounds like it should fire up but it just doesn't catch!!  Anyone have any ideas about the TPS?  I'm thinking that's gotta have something to do with it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mach10||07-22-2001||06:14 PM||||Get a can of alcohol based electronics cleaner, then hose down all the connectors and exposed sensors. Let stand for an hour, the try again. I did this to my Mazda. I eventually had it firing on ONE cylinder. Neatest noise I'd ever heard  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>wump..wump..wump..wump..wump Sounded like a huge lawnmower at idle.<BR>took 25 minutes before the water boiled off whatever, then the next cylinder started firing, then the next, then the next until all four were going again. Funniest (and scariest) thing I'd ever seen.||||reg||10
Z||000008||artherd||07-22-2001||08:31 PM||||Hi Jay, unplug everything, blast the connectors with compressed air, then re-connect using some of the aforementioned "electronics grease"<P>If that doesn't work, you may have permantely fouled a sensor or three and need to replace them.  In particuliar, don't forget to check oxygen sensors (yes, degreaser, etc, can trouble those...)<P>Good Luck!<P>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jay||07-24-2001||12:12 PM||||Thanks everyone, I did all of that and it still didn't fire up.  Waited 2 days and then this morning, turned the key...pressed the ignited starter button and bam!  Started right up!  Tons of smoke poured out and then it settled right down to normal.  I'm back baby!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000010||California Kid||07-24-2001||03:57 PM||||Glad to hear your running again Jay. Don't forget to grease all your electrical connectors. Sounds like the ignition was shorting out, because of all the smoke when it finally fired.||||reg||1
Z||000011||starfighter007@msn.com||07-24-2001||04:13 PM||||yeaaaaaaaa I am really glad for Dont you just love when things go back to the way that there suppose to Ill bet It felt as good as winning the lottery when that bad girl fired up.||||reg||7
Z||000012||Jay||07-25-2001||03:00 PM||||Yeah it felt great, but I was vexed cause I didn't make it to the track.  Now I gotta wait a few weeks to go again.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
